# `picker.recent_commands` lists the commands that RAN (palette, keymap, `:`
# and menu runs alike), newest first, and Enter runs the row again; the empty
# palette pins the same recents first with a ★. It used to read the `:`
# line's history and say `no : lines yet` (walkthrough 1.12).
command picker.recent_commands
expect screen contains "no recent commands yet"
key esc
command editor.suspend_hint
expect screen contains "mnml does not suspend"
key esc
expect screen lacks "mnml does not suspend"
command view.toggle_line_numbers
command picker.recent_commands
expect screen contains "Recent commands"
expect screen contains "Toggle line-number gutter"
expect screen contains "Ctrl+Z suspend not supported"
key esc
command palette
expect screen contains "★ view  ·  Toggle line-number gutter"
key esc
command picker.recent_commands
key down
key enter
expect screen contains "mnml does not suspend"
